 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+The error-handling property below remains outside the scope of usage aggregation in re-cinq/HALEngine#93.
 
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+
+## Turn usage — re-cinq/HALEngine#93
+
+The chosen contract keeps the single usage argument and sums provider calls. Passing both totals and a breakdown is rejected for this change because billing and budgeting need the turn total; a per-call collection would widen the public API without being needed for that contract. The hook parameter/type must explicitly name turn-total semantics. This consumer-visible change requires a MINOR version bump and a changelog entry explaining that tool-heavy turns now record larger, complete totals.
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once after the round loop and receives the component-wise sum of usage from every provider call, including both tool rounds and the final answer. ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call after two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L72)).
+- Missing usage in any round contributes nothing; reported rounds still sum, an entirely unmetered turn reports `undefined`, and totals are isolated to each user turn. ([validated by: sums reported rounds despite missing usage and reports nothing for an unmetered turn](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L83)).
+- A turn with no tools retains its existing usage value. ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
